WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.834
Most agencies run outbound across five tools.

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:07.746
One warms the mailboxes, one sends, one holds the replies,

00:00:07.746 --> 00:00:09.297
one holds the pipeline,

00:00:09.297 --> 00:00:12.533
and a spreadsheet tries to keep it all together.

00:00:13.233 --> 00:00:16.294
Datamart Warmup puts all of it in one workspace.

00:00:16.294 --> 00:00:19.100
Here is a quick tour, on a sample workspace.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:21.710
It starts with your mailboxes.

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:25.817
Every inbox you send from sits on one screen, with what it sent today,

00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:28.398
how far its warmup has come, and its health.

00:00:29.298 --> 00:00:33.783
Connect Google or Microsoft in one click, any other host over SMTP,

00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:36.594
or import a whole list from a spreadsheet.

00:00:37.494 --> 00:00:40.182
Open a mailbox and you get the full picture.

00:00:40.182 --> 00:00:42.320
Its health score, its reply target,

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.641
and how many days it has been warming.

00:00:45.541 --> 00:00:51.040
Warmup trades short test emails with mailboxes from other companies in the network,

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:52.564
a little more each day.

00:00:52.564 --> 00:00:54.950
And sending domains checks that SPF,

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.805
DKIM and DMARC are in place.

00:00:57.705 --> 00:01:01.432
Campaigns are a list of contacts, a sequence, and a schedule.

00:01:01.432 --> 00:01:05.342
Running, paused, drafted or finished, they all live in one list.

00:01:06.242 --> 00:01:08.773
Write the first email and the follow ups.

00:01:08.773 --> 00:01:11.303
Each follow up waits the days you choose,

00:01:11.303 --> 00:01:13.217
and replies in the same thread,

00:01:13.217 --> 00:01:15.501
so it reads like a real conversation.

00:01:16.401 --> 00:01:19.098
Once it is running, you watch it send, live.

00:01:19.098 --> 00:01:22.225
Opens, clicks, replies and bounces, as they happen.

00:01:23.125 --> 00:01:26.346
And every lead shows exactly where it is in the sequence.

00:01:27.246 --> 00:01:30.194
Replies from every mailbox land in one inbox,

00:01:30.194 --> 00:01:32.814
threaded, with the mailbox they came to.

00:01:33.714 --> 00:01:36.688
Eli at Hooli wants the deliverability benchmarks.

00:01:36.688 --> 00:01:39.965
It is tagged as a lead, and you can answer right here.

00:01:40.865 --> 00:01:43.361
Templates keep your best replies one click away.

00:01:44.261 --> 00:01:46.447
Contacts holds everyone you reach,

00:01:46.447 --> 00:01:49.082
with a timeline of every email and reply.

00:01:49.982 --> 00:01:54.425
Deliverability rolls bounces, complaints and spam placement into one score,

00:01:54.425 --> 00:01:58.217
and flags the mailbox that is slipping before it hurts the rest.

00:01:59.117 --> 00:02:02.917
Placement tests send a real copy to seed inboxes at Gmail,

00:02:02.917 --> 00:02:04.096
Outlook and Yahoo,

00:02:04.096 --> 00:02:07.437
and show whether it landed in the inbox or in junk.

00:02:08.337 --> 00:02:10.811
Analytics shows what actually works.

00:02:10.811 --> 00:02:13.834
Sends, opens, replies and bounces over time,

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:15.484
and your best campaigns.

00:02:16.383 --> 00:02:18.329
Interested replies become deals.

00:02:18.329 --> 00:02:20.639
Here is the pipeline, from new to won,

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:22.463
with what each stage is worth.

00:02:23.363 --> 00:02:25.347
Tasks keep the follow ups from slipping.

00:02:26.247 --> 00:02:28.658
And meetings shows every call that is booked.

00:02:29.558 --> 00:02:32.601
Integrations connect the tools you already use,

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:35.126
like Zapier, Calendly, Apollo and Clay.

00:02:36.026 --> 00:02:40.207
API keys let your own tools and agents work with the same data.

00:02:41.107 --> 00:02:43.816
The audit log records who changed what, and when.

00:02:44.717 --> 00:02:47.005
Settings is where you manage your team,

00:02:47.005 --> 00:02:49.410
roles and access, and your sending rules.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:53.469
And on every page there is Molty, the AI assistant.

00:02:53.469 --> 00:02:56.753
It already knows which mailboxes need your attention.

00:02:57.803 --> 00:03:00.114
Ask which campaign gets the most replies,

00:03:00.114 --> 00:03:02.368
and it reads your analytics and answers.

00:03:03.268 --> 00:03:06.354
Ask it to pause anything that hurts deliverability.

00:03:06.354 --> 00:03:07.685
It checks the numbers,

00:03:07.685 --> 00:03:10.649
then waits for your OK before it changes a thing.

00:03:11.549 --> 00:03:14.920
It works in Slack too, so your team can work replies together.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:19.309
Warmup, campaigns, one inbox, a CRM, and AI.

00:03:19.309 --> 00:03:23.579
All in one workspace, and it is free, covered by Datamart.

00:03:24.229 --> 00:03:26.853
Start at warmup.dtm.global.
